Method descriptions implemented from the published literature
-------------------------------------------------------------
Errors-in-variables moment correction
  Fuller, W. A. "Measurement Error Models", Wiley Series in Probability and
  Statistics (1987). DOI 10.1002/9780470316665. The correction itself is
  classical and is cited as such; this release contributes only the split-chip
  identification of the reference assay's own error covariance.

Damped oscillatory state-space recurrence
  Boyer, J., Rusch, T. K., Rus, D. "Learning to dissipate energy in oscillatory
  state-space models", arXiv:2505.12171 (2025). DOI 10.48550/arXiv.2505.12171.
  Rusch, T. K., Rus, D. "Oscillatory state-space models", ICLR 2025 oral,
  arXiv:2410.03943. DOI 10.48550/arXiv.2410.03943.
  The implicit-explicit oscillatory discretisation is described in those two
  reports; the recurrence in src/obscal/twin/oscillatory.py follows their stated
  second-order form. The damping variant is the ablation row of the manuscript,
  not a third-party artefact.

Geometric correction factor for transepithelial resistance
  Yeste, J. et al. "Geometric correction factor for transepithelial electrical
  resistance measurements in transwell and microfluidic cell cultures",
  J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys. 49(37):375401 (2016). DOI 10.1088/0022-3727/49/37/375401.
  Applied as a study-constant correction computed from the printed device
  geometry; the functional form used here is an explicit engineering default
  (see the deviations array of claim_to_code.json).

Sirius Red microplate assay format audit
  Szasz, C. et al. Int. J. Mol. Sci. 24(24):17435 (2023). DOI 10.3390/ijms242417435.
  Huang, C.-Y., Lin, W.-L. Future Sci. OA 11(1):2567169 (2025).
  DOI 10.1080/20565623.2025.2567169.

